Because he was so honest, the people of Makkah gave him a beautiful title: "Al-Amin," which means "The Trustworthy One." Merchants trusted him with their goods. Neighbors trusted him with their secrets.

Years later, when Prophet Muhammad ﷺ began to share the message of Islam, some people in Makkah turned against him — yet many of these same people still came to leave their money and valuable belongings with him for safekeeping.

When the time came to leave Makkah for Madinah, he did not forget the trusts people had given him. He asked his beloved cousin, Imam Ali (عليه السلام), to stay behind and return every single item safely to its owner.

This story teaches us that when we are always truthful, people will trust us — even people who do not agree with us.', 'Being honest and trustworthy makes people trust you, even those who disagree with you', (select id from public.stars where number = 1), (select id from public.categories where slug = 'kindness' and deleted_at is null), 'all', 5, 25, '{"cover_emoji":"🤝","gradient":["#FF8AAB","#FFD24D"],"difficulty":"medium","pages":[{"emoji":"🕌","gradient":["#FF8AAB","#FFD24D"]},{"emoji":"🤝","gradient":["#9ADDFF","#0D9EF5"]},{"emoji":"📦","gradient":["#B87EE9","#6E24A8"]},{"emoji":"🌙","gradient":["#6DD99A","#1FB165"]},{"emoji":"⭐","gradient":["#FFD24D","#FFB100"]}],"sequence_events":["People in Makkah call young Muhammad ﷺ ''Al-Amin'' because he never lies.","Merchants and neighbors trust him with their goods and secrets.","Even people who oppose him still leave their valuables with him.","Before leaving for Madinah, he asks Imam Ali to return every trust safely."],"quiz":[{"id":"q1","question":"What title did the people of Makkah give to Prophet Muhammad ﷺ because of his honesty?","options":["Al-Hakeem (The Wise)","Al-Amin (The Trustworthy)","Al-Karim (The Generous)"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q2","question":"Even people who disagreed with the Prophet ﷺ still trusted him with what?","emoji":"📦","options":["Their food","Their homes","Their money and valuable belongings"],"correctIndex":2},{"id":"q3","question":"Who did the Prophet ﷺ ask to return the people''s trusts before leaving Makkah?","options":["Imam Hasan (عليه السلام)","Imam Ali (عليه السلام)","Salman al-Farsi"],"correctIndex":1}],"moral_choice":{"question":"What is the moral of this story?","options":["Being honest and trustworthy makes people trust you, even those who disagree with you","It is okay to lie if it helps you","Only be honest with people you like","Trust is not important in life"],"correctIndex":0},"badge_emoji":"🤝","badge_title":"Trustworthy Star"}'::jsonb, 'published', 0) on conflict (slug) where deleted_at is null do nothing;

But each day, the Prophet ﷺ did the same gentle thing. He carefully cleared the mess with his own hands and continued on his way without a single word of anger.

One morning, something was different. The path was completely clean. Instead of feeling relieved, the Prophet ﷺ felt worried. "Where is my neighbor today? I hope nothing is wrong."

He asked around and learned that his neighbor was very sick. Without hesitation, the Prophet ﷺ gathered some food and kind words, and walked straight to her house to check on her.

When she saw him standing at her door, she was amazed. She had expected anger, but instead she received warmth and care. Her heart was deeply touched.

This beautiful story shows us that we should always answer unkindness with patience and kindness, because kindness can soften even the hardest hearts.', 'Answer unkindness with patience and kindness', (select id from public.stars where number = 1), (select id from public.categories where slug = 'kindness' and deleted_at is null), 'all', 4, 25, '{"cover_emoji":"💛","gradient":["#6DD99A","#1FB165"],"difficulty":"easy","pages":[{"emoji":"🌵","gradient":["#FF8AAB","#FFD24D"]},{"emoji":"😌","gradient":["#6DD99A","#1FB165"]},{"emoji":"❓","gradient":["#9ADDFF","#0D9EF5"]},{"emoji":"🍲","gradient":["#B87EE9","#6E24A8"]},{"emoji":"🤗","gradient":["#FFD24D","#FFB100"]},{"emoji":"💛","gradient":["#FF8AAB","#FFD24D"]}],"sequence_events":["A neighbor scatters thorns on the path every day.","The Prophet stays calm and clears them without anger.","One day the path is clean — no thorns at all.","He learns she is sick and visits her with kindness."],"quiz":[{"id":"q1","question":"What did the unkind neighbor scatter on the Prophet''s ﷺ path every day?","emoji":"🌵","options":["Flowers","Thorns and garbage","Stones"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q2","question":"How did the Prophet ﷺ respond to this unkindness?","options":["He got angry and complained","He stayed calm and patient","He avoided that path forever"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q3","question":"What did the Prophet ﷺ do when he learned his neighbor was sick?","options":["He ignored her","He visited her with kindness and food","He waited for her to apologize first"],"correctIndex":1}],"moral_choice":{"question":"What is the moral of this story?","options":["Answer unkindness with patience and kindness","Ignore people who are unkind forever","Be unkind back to unkind people","Only help people who are nice to you"],"correctIndex":0},"badge_emoji":"💛","badge_title":"Kind Heart"}'::jsonb, 'published', 1) on conflict (slug) where deleted_at is null do nothing;

The Holy Kaaba had been damaged and needed to be rebuilt. When it came time to place the sacred Black Stone back into its wall, every clan of Makkah wanted the honor of doing it themselves. Tempers grew hotter.

Finally, the elders agreed: whoever walked through the gate next would decide how to solve the problem. As fate would have it, the next person to walk in was Muhammad ﷺ — the one everyone already called Al-Amin.

He asked for a large cloth, placed the Black Stone gently in its center, and invited one leader from each clan to hold an edge together. All of them lifted the stone at the same time, sharing the honor equally.

Everyone was pleased. No one felt left out, and a terrible conflict was avoided completely through wisdom and fairness.', 'Wisdom and fairness can solve conflicts peacefully', (select id from public.stars where number = 1), (select id from public.categories where slug = 'kindness' and deleted_at is null), 'all', 5, 25, '{"cover_emoji":"⚖️","gradient":["#9ADDFF","#0D9EF5"],"difficulty":"hard","pages":[{"emoji":"🕋","gradient":["#9ADDFF","#0D9EF5"]},{"emoji":"⚔️","gradient":["#B87EE9","#6E24A8"]},{"emoji":"🚪","gradient":["#FF8AAB","#FFD24D"]},{"emoji":"🧵","gradient":["#FFD24D","#FFB100"]},{"emoji":"🌟","gradient":["#6DD99A","#1FB165"]}],"sequence_events":["The Black Stone needs to be placed back after the Kaaba is rebuilt.","The clans of Makkah argue over who should have the honor.","They agree the next person through the gate will decide.","Muhammad ﷺ has all clans lift the stone together on a cloth."],"quiz":[{"id":"q1","question":"What sacred object were the clans of Makkah arguing about?","emoji":"🕋","options":["A well of water","The Black Stone (Hajar al-Aswad)","A golden lamp"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q2","question":"How did young Muhammad ﷺ solve the disagreement fairly?","options":["He gave it to the strongest clan","He asked all the clans to lift it together on a cloth","He decided by himself without asking anyone"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q3","question":"Why did the people trust him to make this decision?","options":["He was the richest man in Makkah","He was known as Al-Amin, the trustworthy","He was the oldest man there"],"correctIndex":1}],"moral_choice":{"question":"What is the moral of this story?","options":["Wisdom and fairness can solve conflicts peacefully","Fighting is the only way to settle an argument","Only the strongest should get their way","Problems should be ignored, not solved"],"correctIndex":0},"badge_emoji":"⚖️","badge_title":"Wise Peacemaker"}'::jsonb, 'published', 2) on conflict (slug) where deleted_at is null do nothing;

One day, the Prophet ﷺ was praying in front of his companions. As he lowered himself into sajdah, little Hasan and Husain happily climbed onto his back, giggling as they balanced like it was a fun little ride.

Most people would have gently moved the children away. But not the Prophet ﷺ. Instead, he stayed in that position much longer than usual, patiently waiting so the children would not be startled or fall.

The companions noticed how long the prostration lasted and asked him about it afterward. The Prophet ﷺ smiled and explained that his grandsons had climbed onto his back, and he did not want to disturb their happiness.

This simple, tender moment shows the enormous gentleness and love the Prophet ﷺ had for children, even in the middle of worship.', 'Be gentle, patient, and loving towards children', (select id from public.stars where number = 1), (select id from public.categories where slug = 'kindness' and deleted_at is null), 'all', 4, 25, '{"cover_emoji":"🤗","gradient":["#B87EE9","#6E24A8"],"difficulty":"easy","pages":[{"emoji":"❤️","gradient":["#B87EE9","#6E24A8"]},{"emoji":"🕌","gradient":["#FF8AAB","#FFD24D"]},{"emoji":"⏳","gradient":["#6DD99A","#1FB165"]},{"emoji":"💬","gradient":["#9ADDFF","#0D9EF5"]},{"emoji":"🤗","gradient":["#FFD24D","#FFB100"]}],"sequence_events":["The Prophet ﷺ is praying with his companions.","Hasan and Husain climb onto his back during prostration.","He stays down longer so they will not fall.","He explains afterward that he did not want to disturb them."],"quiz":[{"id":"q1","question":"What did Hasan and Husain (عليهما السلام) do while their grandfather was praying?","emoji":"🤗","options":["They cried loudly","They climbed onto his back during prostration","They ran outside to play"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q2","question":"What did the Prophet ﷺ do when this happened?","options":["He stood up quickly and moved them away","He stayed in prostration longer so they would not fall","He stopped the prayer completely"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q3","question":"What does this story teach us about the Prophet ﷺ?","options":["He did not like being disturbed","He was gentle, patient, and loving towards children","He avoided children during prayer time"],"correctIndex":1}],"moral_choice":{"question":"What is the moral of this story?","options":["Be gentle, patient, and loving towards children","Children should never be near adults who are praying","Interruptions during worship should always be stopped immediately","Only strict rules matter, not kindness"],"correctIndex":0},"badge_emoji":"🤗","badge_title":"Gentle Heart"}'::jsonb, 'published', 3) on conflict (slug) where deleted_at is null do nothing;

The people around were amazed and asked, "O Messenger of Allah, what happened?"

The Prophet ﷺ explained that the camel had complained to him. It told him, through its behavior, that its owner made it work very hard every day but did not feed it enough or give it proper rest.

The Prophet ﷺ asked to see the camel''s owner and spoke to him kindly but firmly, reminding him that animals have feelings too, and asked him to feed the camel properly and never overburden it again.

The owner felt ashamed and promised right away to take much better care of his camel from that day forward.

This touching story reminds us that kindness is not only for people — it must be shown to every living creature Allah has created.', 'Kindness must be shown to animals and all living creatures', (select id from public.stars where number = 1), (select id from public.categories where slug = 'kindness' and deleted_at is null), 'all', 4, 25, '{"cover_emoji":"🐫","gradient":["#FF8AAB","#FFD24D"],"difficulty":"easy","pages":[{"emoji":"🐫","gradient":["#FF8AAB","#FFD24D"]},{"emoji":"😲","gradient":["#9ADDFF","#0D9EF5"]},{"emoji":"💭","gradient":["#6DD99A","#1FB165"]},{"emoji":"🗣️","gradient":["#B87EE9","#6E24A8"]},{"emoji":"🙏","gradient":["#FFD24D","#FFB100"]},{"emoji":"🌟","gradient":["#FF8AAB","#FFD24D"]}],"sequence_events":["The Prophet ﷺ notices a camel making sad sounds in a garden.","He calms the camel and asks what is wrong.","He learns the owner overworks it and does not feed it enough.","He asks the owner to care for the camel properly."],"quiz":[{"id":"q1","question":"Which animal did the Prophet ﷺ show kindness to in this story?","emoji":"🐫","options":["A cat","A camel","A bird"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q2","question":"What was the camel''s problem?","options":["It was too old to walk","It was overworked and not fed properly","It had no owner at all"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q3","question":"What did the Prophet ﷺ ask the owner to do?","options":["Sell the camel to someone else","Take better care of the camel","Leave the camel in the garden forever"],"correctIndex":1}],"moral_choice":{"question":"What is the moral of this story?","options":["Kindness must be shown to animals and all living creatures","Animals do not have feelings","Only people deserve kindness","Working animals hard is always acceptable"],"correctIndex":0},"badge_emoji":"🐫","badge_title":"Animal Friend"}'::jsonb, 'published', 4) on conflict (slug) where deleted_at is null do nothing;

There were no witnesses, and both told their story with total certainty.

Imam Ali (a.s.) listened carefully to every single word, without rushing.

Then he had a clever idea: he asked each one a tiny, specific detail only the true owner would know.

One answered instantly and correctly. The other hesitated and got it wrong.

Justice was done — fairly, wisely, and without anyone needing to raise their voice.', 'Wisdom and fairness solve problems better than guessing', (select id from public.stars where number = 2), (select id from public.categories where slug = 'courage' and deleted_at is null), 'all', 5, 25, '{"cover_emoji":"⚖️","gradient":["#9ADDFF","#0D9EF5"],"difficulty":"medium","pages":[{"emoji":"🧣","gradient":["#9ADDFF","#0D9EF5"]},{"emoji":"❓","gradient":["#6DD99A","#1FB165"]},{"emoji":"👂","gradient":["#FF8AAB","#FFD24D"]},{"emoji":"💡","gradient":["#FFD24D","#FFB100"]},{"emoji":"⚖️","gradient":["#9ADDFF","#0D9EF5"]},{"emoji":"🌟","gradient":["#B87EE9","#6E24A8"]}],"sequence_events":["Two people argue over one blanket.","There are no witnesses to help decide.","Imam Ali listens carefully to both sides.","He asks a clever question that reveals the true owner."],"quiz":[{"id":"q1","question":"What were the two people arguing about?","options":["A horse","A blanket","A house","A ring"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q2","question":"How did Imam Ali (a.s.) figure out the truth?","options":["He guessed","He asked a clever question","He flipped a coin","He asked his friends"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q3","question":"What did Imam Ali (a.s.) do before deciding?","emoji":"👂","options":["Listened carefully to both","Ignored them","Punished both","Left immediately"],"correctIndex":0},{"id":"q4","question":"What made this a fair decision?","options":["It favored the loudest person","It was based on a clever, honest test","It was random","It took the least time"],"correctIndex":1}],"moral_choice":{"question":"What does this story teach us?","options":["Always believe whoever speaks first","Wisdom and fairness solve problems better than guessing","Arguments can never be solved","Only judges can be fair"],"correctIndex":1},"badge_emoji":"⚖️","badge_title":"Wisdom Star"}'::jsonb, 'published', 5) on conflict (slug) where deleted_at is null do nothing;

But their new home held only a few simple things: a soft bed made of sheepskin, a water skin for drinking, a hand mill for grinding grain, and a simple curtain for the door. That was all.

Fatima (سلام الله عليها) never once complained about not having fine furniture. She was happy and grateful with what Allah had given her, because true happiness does not come from possessions.

The Prophet ﷺ himself blessed this humble home with his prayers, and it became one of the most loved households in all of Islam — because of the love and faith of the people living there.

This story teaches us that true richness is found in gratitude and contentment, not in expensive things.', 'True happiness comes from gratitude, not expensive things', (select id from public.stars where number = 3), (select id from public.categories where slug = 'generosity' and deleted_at is null), 'all', 4, 25, '{"cover_emoji":"💍","gradient":["#B87EE9","#6E24A8"],"difficulty":"easy","pages":[{"emoji":"💍","gradient":["#B87EE9","#6E24A8"]},{"emoji":"🏠","gradient":["#FF8AAB","#FFD24D"]},{"emoji":"🙏","gradient":["#6DD99A","#1FB165"]},{"emoji":"🌟","gradient":["#9ADDFF","#0D9EF5"]},{"emoji":"✨","gradient":["#FFD24D","#FFB100"]}],"sequence_events":["Fatima (س) marries Imam Ali (ع), and people expect a grand celebration.","Their new home has only a few simple, humble items.","Fatima (س) is happy and grateful, never complaining.","Their humble home becomes one of the most loved in Islam."],"quiz":[{"id":"q1","question":"What did Fatima (سلام الله عليها) receive when she married Imam Ali (عليه السلام)?","options":["A grand palace full of gold","A few simple household items","Nothing at all"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q2","question":"How did Fatima (سلام الله عليها) feel about her simple home?","options":["Upset and disappointed","Happy and grateful","Embarrassed"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q3","question":"What does this story teach us?","options":["True richness comes from gratitude and contentment","You must have expensive things to be happy","Only fancy weddings are good weddings"],"correctIndex":0}],"moral_choice":{"question":"What is the moral of this story?","options":["True happiness comes from gratitude, not expensive things","You should always want more than you have","Simple homes are not good enough","Only rich people can be content"],"correctIndex":0},"badge_emoji":"💍","badge_title":"Content Heart"}'::jsonb, 'published', 6) on conflict (slug) where deleted_at is null do nothing;

The hard work made her hands tired and sore. One day, she heard her father, Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, had received some helpers, and she hoped one could ease her work.

She went to her father''s house to ask, but he was not home. Later that night, the Prophet ﷺ came to visit Fatima (سلام الله عليها) and Imam Ali (عليه السلام) himself.

He sat between them and said, "Shall I not teach you something better than a servant?" Then he taught them to say "SubhanAllah" 33 times, "Alhamdulillah" 33 times, and "Allahu Akbar" 34 times before sleeping.

Fatima (سلام الله عليها) said this brought her more comfort than any servant. To this day, Muslims everywhere say these same words every night, calling it the "Tasbih of Fatima" in her honor.', 'Remembering Allah brings more comfort than material things', (select id from public.stars where number = 3), (select id from public.categories where slug = 'generosity' and deleted_at is null), 'all', 5, 25, '{"cover_emoji":"🌾","gradient":["#6DD99A","#1FB165"],"difficulty":"medium","pages":[{"emoji":"🌾","gradient":["#FF8AAB","#FFD24D"]},{"emoji":"😔","gradient":["#6DD99A","#1FB165"]},{"emoji":"🚪","gradient":["#9ADDFF","#0D9EF5"]},{"emoji":"🤲","gradient":["#B87EE9","#6E24A8"]},{"emoji":"🌙","gradient":["#FFD24D","#FFB100"]}],"sequence_events":["Fatima (س) works hard every day grinding wheat and caring for her home.","She hopes to ask her father for a servant to help her.","The Prophet ﷺ visits and offers something better than a servant.","He teaches her a special dhikr to say before sleeping."],"quiz":[{"id":"q1","question":"What made Fatima''s (سلام الله عليها) hands tired every day?","emoji":"🌾","options":["Sewing clothes","Grinding wheat by hand","Painting"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q2","question":"What did the Prophet ﷺ teach her instead of giving a servant?","options":["A special song","A special dhikr to say before sleeping","A new recipe"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q3","question":"What is this dhikr called today, in her honor?","options":["The Prayer of Ali","The Tasbih of Fatima","The Dua of Hasan"],"correctIndex":1}],"moral_choice":{"question":"What is the moral of this story?","options":["Remembering Allah brings more comfort than material things","Hard work should always be avoided","Only servants can bring peace of mind","Complaining is the best solution to hard work"],"correctIndex":0},"badge_emoji":"🤲","badge_title":"Devoted Heart"}'::jsonb, 'published', 7) on conflict (slug) where deleted_at is null do nothing;

Soon, Hasan and Husain got better, and true to their promise, the whole family began their three days of fasting — going without food or water from morning until sunset.

On the first evening, just as they were about to break their fast with a little barley bread, a poor man knocked asking for food. Without hesitating, the family gave him their entire meal.

The same thing happened the second night with an orphan, and the third night with a traveler in need. Each night, the family gave away their food completely, staying hungry themselves.

Even though they were weak from fasting, their hearts were full of joy, because they had helped others in need. This example still teaches families the true meaning of generosity.', 'True generosity means giving even when you have very little yourself', (select id from public.stars where number = 3), (select id from public.categories where slug = 'generosity' and deleted_at is null), 'all', 5, 25, '{"cover_emoji":"🍞","gradient":["#9ADDFF","#0D9EF5"],"difficulty":"medium","pages":[{"emoji":"🤒","gradient":["#9ADDFF","#0D9EF5"]},{"emoji":"🌅","gradient":["#6DD99A","#1FB165"]},{"emoji":"🍞","gradient":["#B87EE9","#6E24A8"]},{"emoji":"🚪","gradient":["#FF8AAB","#FFD24D"]},{"emoji":"💖","gradient":["#FFD24D","#FFB100"]}],"sequence_events":["Hasan and Husain get sick, and the family promises to fast three days if they recover.","The children recover, and the family begins their three days of fasting.","Each evening, someone in need knocks at the door asking for food.","The family gives away their entire meal every night, staying hungry themselves."],"quiz":[{"id":"q1","question":"Why did the family decide to fast for three days?","options":["Because it was a special holiday","To thank Allah after Hasan and Husain recovered from being sick","Because they had no food"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q2","question":"What did the family do each night when someone in need came to the door?","emoji":"🍞","options":["They turned them away","They gave away their entire meal","They gave only half their food"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q3","question":"How did the family feel even though they stayed hungry?","options":["Angry and upset","Joyful because they helped others","Regretful"],"correctIndex":1}],"moral_choice":{"question":"What is the moral of this story?","options":["True generosity means giving even when you have very little yourself","You should only give away food you don''t want","Helping others is only for rich people","Promises to Allah don''t need to be kept"],"correctIndex":0},"badge_emoji":"🍞","badge_title":"Generous Heart"}'::jsonb, 'published', 8) on conflict (slug) where deleted_at is null do nothing;

Whenever Fatima (سلام الله عليها) walked into a room where her father was sitting, the Prophet ﷺ would stand up out of respect, walk toward her, kiss her forehead, and seat her in his own place.

He often said that Fatima (سلام الله عليها) was a part of him, and that whoever pleased her pleased him too. He treated her with the deepest honor, even though she was his own child.

Fatima (سلام الله عليها) loved and respected her father just as deeply. She cared for him, comforted him during difficult times, and always sought his happiness.

This beautiful relationship between father and daughter teaches us how important it is to love, respect, and honor our parents and our children with kindness every single day.', 'We should love, respect, and honor our parents and children with kindness', (select id from public.stars where number = 3), (select id from public.categories where slug = 'generosity' and deleted_at is null), 'all', 4, 25, '{"cover_emoji":"💞","gradient":["#FF8AAB","#FFD24D"],"difficulty":"easy","pages":[{"emoji":"🚶","gradient":["#FF8AAB","#FFD24D"]},{"emoji":"❤️","gradient":["#B87EE9","#6E24A8"]},{"emoji":"💬","gradient":["#9ADDFF","#0D9EF5"]},{"emoji":"🤗","gradient":["#6DD99A","#1FB165"]},{"emoji":"💞","gradient":["#FFD24D","#FFB100"]}],"sequence_events":["The Prophet ﷺ always visits Fatima''s (س) home first after a journey.","He stands and shows great respect whenever she enters a room.","He says whoever pleases her pleases him too.","Fatima (س) loves and honors her father deeply in return."],"quiz":[{"id":"q1","question":"Where did the Prophet ﷺ go first after returning from a journey?","options":["The mosque","Fatima''s (سلام الله عليها) home","The marketplace"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q2","question":"What did the Prophet ﷺ do whenever Fatima (سلام الله عليها) entered a room?","options":["He ignored her","He stood up out of respect for her","He asked her to leave"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q3","question":"What did the Prophet ﷺ say about pleasing Fatima (سلام الله عليها)?","options":["It did not matter to him","Whoever pleases her pleases him too","He never spoke about her"],"correctIndex":1}],"moral_choice":{"question":"What is the moral of this story?","options":["We should love, respect, and honor our parents and children with kindness","Respect is only for strangers, not family","Parents should not show love to their children","Honor only matters outside the home"],"correctIndex":0},"badge_emoji":"💞","badge_title":"Loving Heart"}'::jsonb, 'published', 9) on conflict (slug) where deleted_at is null do nothing;

She loved these quiet hours because it was a special time to talk to Allah without any distractions — just her heart, her prayers, and her Lord.

Fatima (سلام الله عليها) prayed for so long, and with such devotion, that sometimes her feet became tired from standing. Yet she never stopped, because her love for worship was stronger than her tiredness.

She also prayed for her neighbors and for people she had never even met, asking Allah to bless and guide them, even before praying for herself.

Because of her incredible devotion, she became known as one of the most worshipful women in history, an example for children and grown-ups alike who wish to grow closer to Allah.', 'True devotion means worshipping Allah with love, even when it is tiring', (select id from public.stars where number = 3), (select id from public.categories where slug = 'generosity' and deleted_at is null), 'all', 4, 25, '{"cover_emoji":"🌙","gradient":["#9ADDFF","#0D9EF5"],"difficulty":"medium","pages":[{"emoji":"🌙","gradient":["#9ADDFF","#0D9EF5"]},{"emoji":"🤲","gradient":["#6DD99A","#1FB165"]},{"emoji":"⏳","gradient":["#B87EE9","#6E24A8"]},{"emoji":"🕊️","gradient":["#FF8AAB","#FFD24D"]},{"emoji":"⭐","gradient":["#FFD24D","#FFB100"]}],"sequence_events":["While Madinah sleeps, Fatima (س) quietly rises to pray at night.","She speaks softly to Allah in the stillness, away from distractions.","She prays so long that her feet become tired, but she never stops.","She prays for her neighbors and others before even praying for herself."],"quiz":[{"id":"q1","question":"When did Fatima (سلام الله عليها) love to pray?","options":["Only during the day","Quietly at night while others slept","Never"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q2","question":"What happened because of her long, devoted prayers?","emoji":"⏳","options":["Nothing happened","Her feet became tired from standing so long","She stopped praying"],"correctIndex":1},{"id":"q3","question":"Who did she often pray for, even before herself?","options":["Only her own family","Her neighbors and people she had never met","No one else"],"correctIndex":1}],"moral_choice":{"question":"What is the moral of this story?","options":["True devotion means worshipping Allah with love, even when it is tiring","Prayer is only important sometimes","We should only pray for ourselves","Worship should be avoided if it is hard"],"correctIndex":0},"badge_emoji":"🤲","badge_title":"Devoted Worshipper"}'::jsonb, 'published', 10) on conflict (slug) where deleted_at is null do nothing;

A crowd gathered, waiting to see if he would shout back.

Instead, Imam Hasan (a.s.) stayed calm and quiet, breathing slowly.

When the man finished, Imam Hasan (a.s.) smiled and offered him help instead of anger.

The man was stunned — he expected a fight, but received only peace.

